    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1123">

                <pb facs="1152" n="1142" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1142"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.115/10–449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >McConaughy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-04">October 4,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received October 3—11:53 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4156. SS <hi rendition="#italic">Flying Trader</hi> arrived Shanghai; made fast
                    Shanghai–Hongkew wharf 1630 hours local time October 3. Master informed
                    Pattison, Isbrandtsen agent, that while anchored outside he had received all
                    wireless messages on the air concerning <hi rendition="#italic">Flying
                        Independent</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Clipper</hi>’, knew those ships
                    had gone southward under guard and <pb facs="1153" n="1143" xml:id="pg1143"/>
                    decided that while Chinese warships were escorting 2 other Isbrandtsen ships
                    time was appropriate to proceed Shanghai in accordance owners’ instructions. In
                    order not attract attention he withheld sending Shanghai agent ETA<anchor n="77"
                        xml:id="d1123-f1"/> by radio until he was well up Yangtze towards Woosung.
                    Cargo aboard for Shanghai about 3000 tons.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Canton 1146, Hong Kong 293, Taipei 336.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McConaughy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
